          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Schur’s lemma is one of the fundamental facts of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+theory"} representation theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-sets"} hom-sets
            between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreducible+representations"} irreducible
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+representations"} linear representations
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groups"} groups
          %p The lemma consists of two parts that depend on different assumptions (a distinction often not highlighted in the literature):
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                The first statement applies over
                %em every
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
              %p
                It says that there are no non-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+morphism"} zero
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
                between distinct (i.e. non-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"}> isomorphic
                )
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreducible+representations"} irreducible representations
                and any non-zero morphism among isomorphic irreducibles is an isomorphism.
            %li
              %p
                The second statement applies only in the special case that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
                is an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraically+closed+field"} algebraically closed field
                (such as the
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representations"} representations
                are
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+dimensional+vector+space"} finite-dimensional
              %p
                It says that, in this case, moreover the only non-trivial
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endomorphisms"} endomorphisms
                of an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreducible+representation"} irreducible representation
                are multiples of the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphism"} identity morphism
          %h2#statement Statement
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %em representation
                means
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+representation"} linear representation
                    of
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
            %li
              %p
                %em finite dimensional representation
                means that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
                is a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite-dimensional+vector+space"} finite-dimensional vector space
            %li
              %p
                an
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreducible+representation"} irreducible representation
                is one whose only
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant"} invariant
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspaces"} subspaces
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+point+spaces"}> fixed point spaces
                ) are the trivial degenerate cases: the
                = succeed "-subspace" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+object"} zero
          %p
          #SchurLemma.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (Schur’s lemma)
              %br/
            %ol
              %li#FirstItem
                %p
                  A
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi V
                        %mo →
                        %mi W
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \;\colon\; V\to W
                  between
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreducible+representations"} irreducible representations
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+morphism"} zero morphism
                  or an
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
                %p
                  It follows that the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endomorphism+ring"} endomorphism ring
                  of an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreducible+representation"} irreducible representation
                  is a
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/division+ring"} division ring
              %li#SecondItem
                %p
                  In the case that the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
                  is an
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraically+closed+field"} algebraically closed field
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endomorphisms"} endomorphisms
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi V
                        %mo →
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \;\colon\; V \to V
                  of a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite-dimensional+vector+space"} finite dimensional
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreducible+representations"} irreducible representations
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                  are multiples
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mi id
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \cdot id
                  of the
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphism"} identity operator
                %p
                  In other words, nontrivial automorphisms of irreducible representations,
                  %em a priori
                  possible by
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "#FirstItem"} (1)
            %p
          %h2#proof Proof
          %p
            As it goes with very fundamental lemmas, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proof"} proof
            of Schur’s lemma follows by elementary inspection.
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              (of Prop.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SchurLemma"}
              %br/
              For the first statement:
            %p
              It is immediate to see that both the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
              as well as
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi f
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    V \overset{f}{\longrightarrow} W
            %p
              of any
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representations"} representations
              are
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant"} invariant
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspaces"} subspaces
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+point+spaces"}> fixed point spaces
              ). But by the very definition of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreducible+representation"} irreducibility
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              are the degenerate ones: their zero subspaces and the full spaces themselves.
            %p
              Now if the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
              is all of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              or the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+object"} zero
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+morphism"} zero morphism
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+object"} zero
              %em and
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
              is all of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+map"} injective
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjective+map"} surjective
              and is hence an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            %p For the second statement:
            %p
              Now we use that over an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraically+closed+field"} algebraically closed field
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              of every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+map"} linear
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endomorphism"} endomorphism
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+dimensional+vector+space"} finite dimensional vector space
              has an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eigenvalue"} eigenvalue
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in k
              (which is, ultimately, due to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+theorem+of+algebra"} fundamental theorem of algebra
              for
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraically+closed+fields"} algebraically closed fields
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              also the linear combination
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo −
                    %mi c
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} id
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi V
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (f - c \cdot \mathrm{id}) \;\colon\; V \longrightarrow V
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              of
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representations"} representations
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              or
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+morphism"} zero
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eigenvectors"} eigenvectors
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eigenvalue"} eigenvalue
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
              are in the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+morphism"} zero
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo −
                    %mi c
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi id
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f - c \cdot id = 0
            %p and hence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo =
                    %mi c
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi id
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f = c \cdot id
            %p is a multiple of the identity.
          %h2#InterpretationInCategoricalAlgebra Interpretation in categorical algebra
          %p
            The statement of
            %em Schur’s lemma
            is particularly suggestive in the language of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+algebra"} categorical algebra
          %p
            Here it says that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreducible+representations"} irreducible representations
            form a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorification"} categorified
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+basis"} orthogonal basis
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-Hilbert+space"} 2-Hilbert space
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite-dimensional+vector+space"} finite-dimensional
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representations"} representations
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthonormal+basis"} orthonormal basis
            if the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraically+closed+field"} algebraically closed
          %p
            After
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decategorification"} decategorification
            this becomes equivalently the statement that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+classes"} isomorphism classes
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreducible+representations"} irreducible representations
            form an
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+basis"} orthogonal basis
            for the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+ring"} representation ring
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthonormal+basis"} orthonormal basis
            if the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraically+closed+field"} algebraically closed
          %p
            For more on this perspective see also at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gram-Schmidt+process"} Gram-Schmidt process
            the section
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "Gram-Schmidt+process#CategorifiedGramSchmidtProcess"} Categorified Gram-Schmidt process
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p We now explain this perspective of in more detail:
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            Notice that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-sets"} hom-sets
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+representations"} category of representations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mi Rep
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G Rep
            are canonically
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi V
                  %mo →
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g \;\colon\; V \to W
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representations"} representations
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+combination"} linear combination
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 1
                  %mi f
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 2
                  %mi g
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi V
                  %mo →
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_1 f + c_2 g \;\colon\; V \to W
            is a
            = succeed "-homomorphism." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mi Rep
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G Rep
            is canonically
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched
            over
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"} Vect
          %p
            Now it makes sense to regard this
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-functor"} hom-functor
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mi Rep
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G Rep
            as analogous
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi hom
                    %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi G
                  %msup
                    %mi Rep
                    %mi op
                  %mo ×
                  %mi G
                  %mi Rep
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi Vect
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  hom_G(-,-) \;\colon\; G Rep^{op} \times G Rep \longrightarrow Vect
          %p
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorification"} categorified
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+product"} inner product
            (see at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-Hilbert+space"} 2-Hilbert space
            for more on this).
          %p
            This is a useful perspective even after
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decategorification"} decategorification
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi W
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi G
                  %msup
                    %mi Rep
                    %mi fin
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V, W \in G Rep^{fin}
            two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite-dimensional+vector+space"} finite-dimensional
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representations"} representations
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi dim
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi hom
                    %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\langle V,W\rangle
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  dim\big( hom_G(V,W) \big)
                  \\;\in\;
                  \\mathbb{N}
          %p
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            of the vector space of homomorphism between them (e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#tomDieck09"} tom Dieck 09, p. 29
          %p
            This construction only depends on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+classes"} isomorphism classes
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
